# OPC UA deep packet inspection rules.
#
# OPC UA is the dominant machine-to-machine protocol for OT/IT convergence
# (historians, MES, cloud gateways). Suricata has no OPC UA application-layer
# parser, so these rules match the OPC UA TCP message header: a 3-byte message
# type (HEL, ACK, ERR, RHE, OPN, MSG, CLO) followed by a 1-byte chunk type
# (F = final, C = intermediate, A = abort).
#
# Conventions (see rules/native/README.md):
#   - sid range 9000000-9000099 is reserved for this repository
#   - metadata carries attack_ics <technique> for the generated coverage map
#
# Approved OPC UA clients: 172.21.0.20 and 172.22.0.10. OPC UA servers live in
# 172.31.0.0/24 on port 4840.

# OPN = OpenSecureChannel. A secure-channel request from outside the approved
# client set is a remote-services / unauthorised-session signal.
alert tcp [!172.21.0.20,!172.22.0.10] any -> 172.31.0.0/24 4840 (msg:"OT OPC UA OpenSecureChannel From Unauthorized Client"; flow:to_server,established; content:"|4F 50 4E|"; depth:3; classtype:policy-violation; metadata: attack_ics T0886, detection_status experimental; reference:url,attack.mitre.org/techniques/T0886/; sid:9000008; rev:1;)

# HEL = Hello, the first message of any OPC UA TCP session. Catches a connection
# attempt from an unapproved host before the secure channel is established.
alert tcp [!172.21.0.20,!172.22.0.10] any -> 172.31.0.0/24 4840 (msg:"OT OPC UA Hello From Unapproved Client"; flow:to_server,established; content:"|48 45 4C|"; depth:3; classtype:policy-violation; metadata: attack_ics T0886, detection_status experimental; reference:url,attack.mitre.org/techniques/T0886/; sid:9000009; rev:1;)
